I'll design and run a clean Ollivier-Ricci measurement on prime-Cayley graphs vs. matched random Cayley controls. Skipping further WebFetch since I have the standard definition: for graph G with simple random walk, $m_x$ uniform on $N(x)$, and edge $(x,y)$, $\kappa(x,y) = 1 - W_1(m_x, m_y)/d(x,y)$. By translation invariance on $\text{Cay}(\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}, S)$, $\kappa$ depends only on the generator $g = y - x \in S$, so $|S|/2$ distinct values per graph.
